    "created_at": "2014-10-01T05:12:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2014-10-01T05:12:10Z",
    "body": "The first comment was about `ReadableStream`, We can think of similar issue about `WritableStream`. I.e. `abort()`-ing a `WritableStream` while allowing the underlying sink to drain the queued data. We can realize this by watching for the Promise returned by the last `write()` call, and call `abort()` when the Promise is fulfilled.\n\nFor `ReadableStream`, we need help by `strategy` to watch for completion of draining.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
